# RecorderMore

TLC reached more states than the chart budget of 500, so the chart draws only the bug paths: 7 states and 8 arrows.

## R08_SurfacesAgree breaks
The shortest path has 8 steps:
0. Not recording | gate off in the page
1. you click (click 1): it reaches the page untouched and starts a navigation: Not recording | gate off in the page | navigation under way | click 1: reached the page; report on its way; not in the timeline
2. the new page loads: Not recording | gate off in the page | on the new page | click 1: reached the page; report on its way; not in the timeline | toolbar shows loading, window shows off
3. the recorder answers the new page's question about the state: Not recording | gate off in the page | on the new page | click 1: reached the page; report on its way; not in the timeline | toolbar shows loading, window shows off
4. you press Record: Recording | gate off in the page (switch-on on its way) | on the new page | click 1: reached the page; report on its way; not in the timeline | toolbar shows loading, window shows off
5. the recorder announces its new state: Recording | gate off in the page (switch-on on its way) | on the new page | click 1: reached the page; report on its way; not in the timeline | toolbar shows loading, window shows off
6. the announcement reaches the toolbar: Recording | gate off in the page (switch-on on its way) | on the new page | click 1: reached the page; report on its way; not in the timeline | toolbar shows recording, window shows off
7. that answer reaches the toolbar: Recording | gate off in the page (switch-on on its way) | on the new page | click 1: reached the page; report on its way; not in the timeline
8. the window catches up: Recording | gate off in the page (switch-on on its way) | on the new page | click 1: reached the page; report on its way; not in the timeline | toolbar shows off, window shows recording

